## Test Smell Audit — Academic Catalog (testsmells.org)

**Target:** `DataAccess.IntegrationTests/UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`  
**Framework:** MSTest 4.1 (.NET 10)  
**Calibration:** Integration-test rules applied (`[TestCategory("Integration")]` detected)

---

### Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Total    | 4           | 4              |

---

### Findings by Severity

#### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` line 113  
**Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
    // ← No assertion — passes even if data is silently corrupt
}
```

**Risk:** False confidence — 100% pass rate regardless of whether inserts actually persist.  
**Fix:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count, "All bulk-inserted users should be persisted");
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` line 94  
**Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType`

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Risk:** One branch is never exercised — the test "passes" but silently skips half its logic. If the type hierarchy changes, the test adapts without failing.  
**Fix:** Split into two explicit tests:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenStandard_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_WhenPremium_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("eve@example.com", "Eve", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = (PremiumUser)_repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com")!;
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0, "Premium users must have a positive discount");
}
```

---

#### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` line 87  
**Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay`

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // 3-second hard wait
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Integration calibration note:** Even for integration tests, hard sleeps are a smell — they cause slow suites and timing-dependent failures in CI.  
**Risk:** Flaky under load; adds 3 s to every run regardless of actual notification speed.  
**Fix:** Use polling with a timeout:
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await WaitUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification should be sent within timeout");
}

private static async Task<bool> WaitUntilAsync(Func<bool> condition, TimeSpan timeout)
{
    var deadline = DateTime.UtcNow + timeout;
    while (DateTime.UtcNow < deadline)
    {
        if (condition()) return true;
        await Task.Delay(100);
    }
    return false;
}
```

---

#### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` line 28  
**Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase`

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
// ← 4 assertions, zero message parameters
```

**Risk:** When one fails in CI, the output is `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` with no context about which property or why.  
**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip through persistence");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip through persistence");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Persisted user should receive a positive auto-increment ID");
```

---

### ✅ Smell-Free Patterns (Well-Written Tests)

| Method | Why it's good |
|--------|---------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange/act/assert, focused scope |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Single assertion proves the behavior |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count (3) is self-documenting after 3 inserts |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Good concurrency integration pattern with clear assertion |

The fixture (`[TestInitialize]`) uses in-memory SQLite — no **Mystery Guest** smell since no external resource dependency exists. All fields are used by every test — no **General Fixture** smell.

---

### Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Effort | Action |
|----------|-------|--------|--------|
| 1 | Assertion-Free Test | ~5 min | Add count assertion to `BulkInsert` |
| 2 | Conditional Test Logic | ~10 min | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into two tests |
| 3 | Sleepy Test | ~15 min | Replace `Thread.Sleep` with polling helper |
| 4 | Assertion Roulette | ~5 min | Add message strings to `InsertUser` assertions |

**Bottom line:** 4 of 8 tests are clean. The 3 high-severity findings (assertion-free, conditional logic, hard sleep) directly risk false passes or flaky CI failures. The assertion roulette is lower priority but quick to fix.
